# sw_only regression baseline -- mgc_fft_a
#
# Produced by:  test/regress/run_regress.sh --update-baselines
# Config:       test/regress/configs/mgc_fft_a.toml  (frozen; changes with this file)
# Recorded:     2026-08-18 at commit 26ba16e
# Reason:       TWO bundled sw_only behaviour changes (Mark authorized both; the 2026-08-17 freeze requires an explicit decision and this is it). (1) TODO #32/7a+7b: best-solution tracking moved onto the lookahead v_k. snapshotBestPlacement stores next.probe_pos and recordIterationResults measures HPWL at probe (new at_probe arg on computeTotalWirelength/computeWirelength_HPWL), so HPWL, overflow and the stored solution all describe ONE position -- XPlace has a single position variable (p IS v_k, nesterov_optimizer.py:71) and evaluator_fn measures both metrics there (run_placement_nesterov.py:142-145). BEST_SOL_MIN_ITER is now phaseIteration() not absolute iteration, matching param_scheduler.py:393 where init_iter resets at each optimizer restart. Also folded syncProbeToCommitted into restoreBestPlacement (restores BOTH node_pos and probe_pos) and deleted it -- verified bit-exact on all three designs, so the perturbation its comment claimed (mms_adaptec1 1325->1288) does not reproduce. (2) TODO #3 fixed-density cap-vs-scale: Grid::clampFixedDensity now SCALES saturated fixed occupancy by target_density, min(overlap,bin_area)*td, matching XPlace initializer.py:82 min(rho,1)*td. It previously CAPPED at min(rho,td), which reads high in macro-perimeter bins at td<1 (at td=0.65, rho=0.5: XPlace 0.325 vs ours 0.50). Identical at td=1. 28-design suite re-run in the same change.
#
# DO NOT refresh this file to make a failing test pass. Read the diff first: the
# body below is the full per-iteration trajectory, so the row where it starts to
# differ tells you what changed and when. See test/regress/README.md.
